    "quote": "Let $G=(V,E)$ be a directed graph. If $G$ contains a $k$-packing independent set $S$ with $\\abs{S}\\ge 2$, then for any randomized algorithm and any time horizon $T$, there exists a sequence of loss functions such that the expected regret is $\\Omega\\tp{\\max\\set{\\frac{|S|}{k},\\log |S|}^{\\frac{1}{3}}\\cdot T^{\\frac{2}{3}}}$."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Restated as Theorem 11. Proof assumes |S| and T sufficiently large; hard instances are stochastic Bernoulli losses."
